    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table, following the existing pattern for read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are code-generated from this spec at build time), documenting the fixed table and the `UNKNOWN` fallback.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - A `CITY_REGION` lookup map (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`).\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(toLocality(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `toLocality(Owner)` default method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\n`locality` is a purely derived value computed at mapping time from `city`, so no entity/DB column was needed \u2014 matching how the other derived owner fields work.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW`) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) both pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
